  "id": "DrugBank_DB00291 - MONDO_2083",
  "verbalization": "Chlorambucil, through its indication for Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia (ALL), links to Ofatumumab and Obinutuzumab, both of which are indicated for Richter Syndrome. This suggests a potential pathway where Chlorambucil may influence the progression of ALL, which in turn could contribute to the development of Richter Syndrome. The evidence is supported by the shared indication for ALL in Path 2 and 3, and the subsequent indication for Richter Syndrome in both cases. The final score of 0.6426 in Path 1 further reinforces the connection between Chlorambucil and Richter Syndrome via Follicular Lymphoma, which is also indicated for Duvelisib, another agent linked to Richter Syndrome. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Chlorambucil in the treatment or pathogenesis of Richter Syndrome through its influence on ALL and its downstream effects on lymphoma progression.",
